p",50.71399,-127.40594,"Cattle Islands (BCMT)",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Shell, sand beach. Sheltered, undeveloped. Large forested upland site reached from N end of beach along shell trail. Suited to small groups. Additional beach camping except at Springs. Attractive."}],["n10074001107","peak",50.26064,-127.3823,"Kashutl",{"ele":"1111"}],["n10105738329","peak",50.99839,-127.49691,"Coast Hill",{"ele":"237"}],["n10105790874","peak",50.93064,-127.39517,"Leading Hill",{"ele":"146"}],["n10105831441","peak",50.83716,-127.57434,"Meeson Cone",{"ele":"142"}],["n10109025035","camp",50.70359,-127.86196,"Nahwitti Lake Recreation Site",{"fee":"no","website":"https://www.sitesandtrailsbc.ca/resource/REC0125"}],["n11009087203","camp",50.90487,-127.53777,"Kent Island (BCMT)",{"website":"https://bcparks.ca/mahpahkum-ahkwuna-deserters-walker-conservancy/","backcountry":"yes","description":"Low gradient sand, gravel, boulder beach protected at all tides. End of the lagoon muddy. Day use. Undeveloped. Sheltered. Camp at top of beach between bushes, above all but highest tides. Level pebbl"}],["n11009087204","camp",50.90122,-127.5357,"Kent Island 2 (BCMT)",{"website":"https://bcparks.ca/mahpahkum-ahkwuna-deserters-walker-conservancy/","backcountry":"yes","description":"Day use. Small stream crosses SW part of beach. Directly to NE of stream,10 m path leads to tent flat behind big cedar. May need brushing. Alternate camp on protected beach. Additional upland potentia"}],["n11009130399","camp",50.80156,-127.63226,"Goletas Waterfall (BCMT)",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Moderate gradient cobble, rocks beach. Boulders. Long carry at low water. All-tide beach camping on pebble. Summer Springs to 5.0 m leave small beach area. Upland sites possible with brushing. Year-ro"}],["n11009146705","camp",50.89974,-127.53412,"Kent Island 3 (BCMT)",{"website":"https://bcparks.ca/mahpahkum-ahkwuna-deserters-walker-conservancy/","backcountry":"yes","description":"Day use. Sheltered, undeveloped. Little beach above high tide. Not a good site, but useful shelter if crossing QC Strait. Might instead be 50Deg 54.063'N 127Deg 32.094'W."}],["n11009239364","camp",50.84424,-127.57542,"Harlequin Bay (BCMT)",{"fee":"no","website":"https://bcparks.ca/gods-pocket-marine-park/","backcountry":"yes","description":"Sand, crushed shell beach. Low tide entrance may be blocked by rocks (fish trap weir?). Sites in 2 mossy forest clearings above steep bank on N side of bay. Wilderness camping allowed. Midden location"}],["n11009239365","camp",50.83802,-127.59361,"Christie Passage (BCMT)",{"website":"https://bcparks.ca/gods-pocket-marine-park/","backcountry":"yes","description":"Dispersed site secondary. Up steep bank 4 M high on obvious midden. 50° 50.278'N 127° 35.618'W. Not visible from main passage. No facilities,Random wilderness camping. No fees charged. Obvious midden "}],["n11009239366","camp",50.83421,-127.52862,"Bell Island (BCMT)",{"fee":"no","website":"https://bcparks.ca/gods-pocket-marine-park/","backcountry":"yes","description":"Protected shell, sand beach. Grassy, partially treed area on an midden shelf above beach. Sheltered. No facilities. Random wilderness camping allowed. Avoid fires except on beach, not on midden. Attra"}],["n11009292307","camp",50.8554,-127.63919,"Balaklava Island Booms (BCMT)",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Sheltered, smooth pebble, shale beach. Back eddy near shore. Former log sort area re-vegetated so needs serious brushing if more than a handful of tents are used. Rustic camp furniture. Attractive. No"}],["n11009292308","camp",50.82971,-127.62267,"Nolan Point (BCMT)",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Low gradient cobble beach. Spacious, sheltered, grassy area between trees, towards point. Afternoon sun. Rustic camp furniture. Seasonal water at creek, to ~june. Attractive, popular site. Short trail"}],["n11009326657","camp",50.78513,-127.57698,"Songhees Creek (BCMT)",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Protected steep cobble, gravel beach. Spacious, semi-exposed camp on level gravel bar. Some protection from NW. Water at creek. Attractive. Road nearby."}],["n11009326658","camp",50.77692,-127.53587,"Goodnuff Beach (BCMT)",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Protected pocket gravel beach at high water, large smooth rocks at low water. E aspect. Small sloped beach margin sites. Dense vegetation in upland. Marginal site but suitable for emergency or transit"}],["n11009326659","camp",50.76041,-127.49129,"Hardy Bay northwest (BCMT)",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Beach. Some protection. Informal site secondary. Level site that has seen previous use."}],["n11049997177","camp",50.90238,-127.29575,"Robinson Pass Low Tide",{"backcountry":"yes","description":"Potential camp site at low tide levels up to maybe 4.2m. Views to strait. Sand / mud / gravel beach on NE side, rocks on SW. Entrance to harbor passable at high tides, perhaps 4.5m+."}],["n11967944755","wc",50.7223,-127.4565,"",{}],["n12117600709","hut",50.69336,-128.36937,"Lowrie Bay Emergency Shelter",{}],["n12117600710","wc",50.69343,-128.36918,"",{}],["n12389464282","wc",50.51135,-128.0293,"",{}],["n12437662928","camp",50.58394,-128.23014,"Raft Cove Backcountry Camping Tentpads",{"fee":"yes","operator":"BC Parks","website":"https://bcparks.ca/raft-cove-park/","backcountry":"yes"}],["n13066492801","wc",50.74492,-127.61342,"",{}],["w175756349","park",50.68489,-127.37793,"",{}],["w184432435","park",50.68531,-128.25111,"",{}],["w313886938","camp",50.4799,-128.09188,"Grant Bay Recreation Site",{"fee":"no","website":"https://vancouverislandnorth.ca/stakeholder/grant-bay-recreation-site/"}],["w313886983","camp",50.39354,-127.20918,"Maynard Lake Recreation Site",{"fee":"no","website":"https://www.sitesandtrailsbc.ca/resource/REC3198"}],["w313887003","camp",50.38665,-127.71876,"O'Connell Lake Recreation Site",{"fee":"no","website":"https://www.sitesandtrailsbc.ca/resource/REC3206"}],["w313887010","camp",50.42955,-127.37018,"Pinch Creek Recr